WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.980
- [Narrator] In the skies
over the Spanish province

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:07.160
of Ciudad Real lies something unexpected

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.550
abandoned silos have been transformed

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.830
into enormous works of art.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.113
Together, they form the world's
largest open-air museum.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.830
But what makes this project truly unique

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.410
are the people that came
together to create it all.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.064
(soft music)

00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:28.981
(speaking Spanish)

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.510
- [Narrator] To create
his giant works of art

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.320
Okuda partnered with an
organization called Laborvalia

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.316
that works with people with
intellectual disabilities.

00:00:41.316 --> 00:00:44.355
(soft, upbeat music)

00:00:44.355 --> 00:00:47.272
(speaking Spanish)

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.250
- [Narrator] What started
as a single mural by Okuda

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.430
has grown to cover 10 different silos

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.697
by artists from around the world.

00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:01.780
(soft, upbeat music)

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.572
The latest step of the
project is to transform

00:01:08.572 --> 00:01:11.698
the interior of one these massive silos.

00:01:11.698 --> 00:01:14.615
(speaking Spanish)

00:01:21.444 --> 00:01:23.080
- [Narrator] But in the end, for Okuda,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.662
it's the creative journey
that's been the most gratifying.

00:01:25.662 --> 00:01:28.579
(speaking Spanish)

00:01:51.058 --> 00:01:53.641
(bell ringing)

